{"base_rate":0.29697766097240474,"brier":0.11073088042049933,"bss":0.4696337920767514,"bss_hi":0.5649627060522924,"bss_lo":0.3795510857801564,"chart":{"base":[318.7,116.1],"fp":[168.1,180.2],"lead":"62,253.3 272,229 482,199 692,157.4","note":{"base":"skill 0.47 — higher than 88% of cities","fp":"low end -3pp, high end +21pp","lead":"day-1 error 1.1 °C — better than 53% of cities","rel":"promised 1% → rained 0%; promised 100% → rained 91%"},"rel":"71.3,466 253.7,433.6 578.8,258.6 691.8,72.8"},"country":"JP","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve","Seasonal split"],"ece":0.1393166885676741,"ess":481.02807530022767,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Tokyo</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Tokyo rain forecast is genuinely useful, though 6 points on its probability scale are off by more than chance explains.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (100%), believe about\n<b>91%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(0%), there is still roughly a <b>0%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 761 days, 2024-04-26 to\n2026-05-31. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nthe station, 5.3 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score 0.47, ranked 26 of\n216 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(8&ndash;64) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>0%</td><td class='num'><b>0%</b></td><td class='num'>192</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>4%</td><td class='num'><b>0%</b></td><td class='num'>103</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>19%</td><td class='num'><b>4%</b></td><td class='num'>81</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>42%</td><td class='num'><b>11%</b></td><td class='num'>79</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>72%</td><td class='num'><b>32%</b></td><td class='num'>75</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>92%</td><td class='num'><b>64%</b></td><td class='num'>75</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>100%</td><td class='num'><b>91%</b></td><td class='num'>156</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">6 of 7 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>Tokyo</b> <span class=\"muted\">Japan</span></p>\n  <div class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag good\">Genuinely useful</span><details class=\"ginfo\"><summary aria-label=\"What does this label mean?\" title=\"What does this label mean?\">?</summary><div class=\"ginfo-pop\" role=\"note\"><p>Compared with a simple guess: saying &ldquo;30% chance of rain&rdquo; every day, because it rains here on 30% of days.</p><p>The forecast did clearly better.</p><p><a href=\"#bss\">How the skill score works</a></p></div></details>\n    <span class=\"muted\">6 points off by more than chance</span></div>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score<details class=\"ginfo\"><summary aria-label=\"What is the skill score?\" title=\"What is the skill score?\">?</summary><div class=\"ginfo-pop\" role=\"note\"><p>How much better the forecast is than that simple guess. 0 means no better, 1 means perfect, below 0 means worse. Day-ahead rain forecasts usually score 0.3 to 0.5.</p><p><a href=\"#bss\">How the skill score works</a></p></div></details></dt><dd>0.47</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>8&ndash;64\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 216</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>761 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    Tokyo &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for Tokyo\"><rect class=\"chart-plot\" x=\"58\" y=\"18\" width=\"354\" height=\"364\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"58\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"382\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"58\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"386\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">0%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"146.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"146.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"291.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"291.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"146.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">25%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"295.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">25%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"235.0\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"235.0\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"200.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"200.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">50%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"204.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">50%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"323.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"323.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"109.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"109.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"323.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">75%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"113.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">75%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"412\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"18\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"412\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">100%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">100%</text><polygon class=\"chart-band\" points=\"58.0553125,380.1041666666667 72.81300970873787,350.19417475728153 126.52740740740742,278.641975308642 205.91822784810125,193.08860759493672 314.5792,81.09333333333336 382.1696,27.70666666666665 411.8865384615384,18.0 411.8865384615384,20.333333333333314 382.1696,71.38666666666666 314.5792,153.89333333333332 205.91822784810125,266.8101265822785 126.52740740740742,341.55555555555554 72.81300970873787,378.4660194174757 58.0553125,382.0\" opacity=\"0.16\"/><line class=\"chart-ideal\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\" stroke-dasharray=\"5,4\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><line class=\"chart-base\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"273.9001314060447\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"273.9001314060447\" stroke-dasharray=\"2,3\"/><polyline class=\"chart-line\" points=\"58.0553125,382.0 72.81300970873787,382.0 126.52740740740742,368.51851851851853 205.91822784810125,340.53164556962025 314.5792,265.52 382.1696,149.04 411.8865384615384,50.666666666666686\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2.4\"/><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 0%&amp;#10;It rained 0% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 192 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"58.0553125\" cy=\"382.0\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 4%&amp;#10;It rained 0% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 103 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"72.81300970873787\" cy=\"382.0\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 19%&amp;#10;It rained 4% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 81 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"126.52740740740742\" cy=\"368.51851851851853\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 42%&amp;#10;It rained 11% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 79 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"205.91822784810125\" cy=\"340.53164556962025\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 72%&amp;#10;It rained 32% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 75 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"314.5792\" cy=\"265.52\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 92%&amp;#10;It rained 64% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 75 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"382.1696\" cy=\"149.04\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 100%&amp;#10;It rained 91% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 156 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"411.8865384615384\" cy=\"50.666666666666686\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"422\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What the forecast promised</text><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"15\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 15 200.0)\">How often it actually rained</text></svg>\n<figcaption>Green band = where a <b>flawless</b> forecast would still land, given\nhow few days we have. Red dots fall outside it, so those are real errors rather\nthan noise. The faint horizontal line is climatology\n(30%).</figcaption></figure>\n","season":"\n<h2 id=\"season\">Does the season matter?</h2>\n<p>In Tokyo the forecast is most skilful in\n<b>spring</b> (0.53) and least in\n<b>summer</b> (0.30).</p>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th>Season</th><th class=\"num\">Days</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Rain days</th><th class=\"num\">Skill score</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Avg error</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>summer</td><td class='num'>184</td><td class='num'>34%</td><td class='num'>0.297</td><td class='num'>18.9%</td></tr><tr><td>winter</td><td class='num'>175</td><td class='num'>11%</td><td class='num'>0.355</td><td class='num'>9.9%</td></tr><tr><td>autumn</td><td class='num'>182</td><td class='num'>35%</td><td class='num'>0.508</td><td class='num'>12.5%</td></tr><tr><td>spring</td><td class='num'>220</td><td class='num'>36%</td><td class='num'>0.533</td><td class='num'>14.2%</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">Four-way splits of a two-year record are thin, so read the\nordering as indicative. Coarser binning is used here than for the annual curve\nfor the same reason.</p>\n"},"lat":35.6895,"lon":139.69171,"n":761,"n_cities":216,"name":"Tokyo","offset_days":0,"pop_map":[{"hi":0.02,"lo":0.0,"mean":0.00015625,"n":192,"obs":0.0,"sig":false},{"hi":0.12,"lo":0.02,"mean":0.041844660194174745,"n":103,"obs":0.0,"sig":true},{"hi":0.29,"lo":0.12,"mean":0.19358024691358028,"n":81,"obs":0.037037037037037035,"sig":true},{"hi":0.59,"lo":0.29,"mean":0.4178481012658228,"n":79,"obs":0.11392405063291139,"sig":true},{"hi":0.84,"lo":0.59,"mean":0.7248,"n":75,"obs":0.32,"sig":true},{"hi":0.99,"lo":0.84,"mean":0.9157333333333333,"n":75,"obs":0.64,"sig":true},{"hi":1.0,"lo":0.99,"mean":0.9996794871794871,"n":156,"obs":0.9102564102564102,"sig":true}],"prcp_km":5.3,"provisional":false,"rank":26,"rank_hi":64.0,"rank_lo":8.0,"reliability":0.037716011545700284,"resolution":0.13360826076669396,"skill_pct":null,"slug":"tokyo","station":"","timezone":"Asia/Tokyo"}